code.description:
A TypeScript module that exports a default async function returning a string; that string is the tool result. Runs at the project root, so import other files by relative path. No top-level `return` (it's a module, not a function body) and no React hooks (not a component). Example:

export default async function () {
  const el = document.querySelector("main");
  return JSON.stringify({ width: el?.clientWidth ?? null });
}
